# The .gitignore of a committed Atoms Worker directory. Runtime-owned:
# `atoms-runtime-cloudflare upgrade` rewrites it, so add project-level ignores
# to your repository's root .gitignore (as `atoms-worker/<path>`) rather than
# here.
#
# Everything the Atoms CLI writes into this directory at build, dev or deploy
# time is listed below, so a deploy never leaves the directory dirty. The
# committed files are the runtime and your wrangler.jsonc; see README.md for
# which is which.

# Written by `atoms deploy` and `atoms dev` from your `atoms build` output
# (scripts/bundle-from-cli.mjs). It embeds your app; regenerate it, never
# commit it.
/src/bundle.generated.js

# Installed by `npm ci` from the committed package-lock.json.
/node_modules/

# The php-wasm runtime, fetched from npm and staged by
# scripts/prepare-runtime.mjs during `npm ci`. It is a large upstream artifact
# under its own licence; the lockfile pins it, and the staging step verifies
# its size and SHA-256. Never commit it.
/.php-wasm/

# The local-dev vehicle for ATOMS_SHARED_SECRET, written by `atoms dev` from
# your app's dotenv file. It is the per-machine root every key on the app <->
# Worker boundary derives from. Never commit it: a committed dev secret is a
# known master key.
/.dev.vars

# Wrangler's own local state (`wrangler dev` storage, logs, caches).
/.wrangler/

# `npm pack` output, if you ever pack this directory.
/dist/
